# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  chief — git carries the TOOLKIT, not your notes.
#
#  A vault fills up with real things: names, calendars, money, health, the
#  half-written thought you would not say out loud. The toolkit is what you
#  would share; the content never is. So this file is default-deny — git
#  sees nothing until a line below names it, and no note is ever named.
#
#  That is a safety rail, not a limitation. Obsidian Sync (or Syncthing, or
#  a private clone with these lines removed) carries the content between
#  your own machines, end to end, without it ever reaching a git remote.
#  Nothing you write here is tracked, so a repo leak exposes none of it.
#
#  The exception is the four filled-in vault files below, because a template
#  nobody can read is not a template. Overwrite them with your own week; every
#  note you add after that is ignored.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/*
!/.claude/
.claude/intel-sources.md
!/.githooks/
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/INSTITUTION.md
!/README.md
!/LICENSE

# The four filled-in notes below are tracked so the template can be read at all.
# They are a starting point, not a place to keep working: once they are yours,
# `git rm --cached` them and everything you write after that is ignored.
!/index.md
!/planner.md
!/fleet.md
!/projects/
!/projects/example/
!/projects/example/status.md
!/archive/
archive/*
!/archive/daily/
archive/daily/*
!/archive/daily/.gitkeep
!/areas/
areas/*
!/areas/.gitkeep
!/inbox/
inbox/*
!/inbox/.gitkeep

# Within the toolkit, still keep secrets, machine-local overrides, and
# transient runtime state out of git.
.claude/secrets.env
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/seen-urls.txt
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/todos
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/projects/
.obsidian/
*.env
